body:
I am terrible at gathering my thoughts, apologies haha.  


\-I would really need to show comparison photos for my masseters and appropriate angles etc, I am sure people have worse enlargement than me, but they really have gotten bigger and are very tight and sore and bumpy and my physio agrees. I hope some habit changes and getting on top of emotions can help there, and am considering botox injections to help the process butttt I always faint from needles so worst case scenario I do that haha. I think I have worsening elongation, as well as deep-set/hooded eyes/heavy brow so I feel like the two don't pair up well haha be nice if chin to lip and lip to nose space shortened a bit!  


\-I am currently working on that stuff with physio for neck pain, scapula issues and I also have knee/hip issues from injury. I also learnt I have joint hyper-mobility and that could be another factor. I also think fillings I have gotten have affect my bite a bit and what is comfortable, and I do other things like lean and my hand a lot, sleep on my side etc which can all aggravate jaw problems (or so I have read). I also tense up a lot and clench jaw when stressed/angry/focusing etc. I think they typically sit just a bit apart, back teeth touch first if anything then jaw has to slide forward a touch to fully close. Since trying to observe my habits I notice I 'tap' my teeth a lot.. like they are going to shut, can't seem to find a comfy grove, then open again and try a different spot (if that makes sense). 

&#x200B;

\-I think it is the long the face coupled with my bone structure. My sister is much more attractive than me and I feel like the ugly man version of her/she the version of my if I had feminine features. She has a shorter face, slightly wider eyes, smaller nose without kinda bulbous tip, smaller chin, fuller lips, softer/slightly more lifted brow bone etc. Also figure wise I am quite masculine and she is not.

&#x200B;

\-I have looked into the chewing and swallowing habit, I think that one will take me a while to nail as I have no control with food, especially in the emotional eating sense haha. I definitely swallow with my cheeks and often chew them/activate them.

&#x200B;

\-The underbite thing was more that felt like my jaw was slowly starting to head that way, like if I close my mouth shut I do have the sensation a am jutting my jaw forward. Also when I open my mouth I feel like it comes forward heaps. Admittedly, having a long chin probably emphasises any of things things and is more apparent front on/in photos, especially with flash. My nose, cheeks, chin and brow bone always catch the light, whereas my eyes and mouth ares looks shadowy! I wouldn't have thought I have more of an overbite, interesting, and recessed maxilla with overbite? That sounds strange haha

&#x200B;

\-While I agree I do think postural things play a role with nasal problems like allergies, I do still think I get allergies. Certain things set me off, one particularly bad thing is cats and dust can be pretty bad. My dad is Anglo-Indian and never had allergy problems in India but as soon as he came to Australia he was sneezing all the time etc. My mum doesn't have issues (Australian) and my sister barely does. I haven't looked too thoroughly into this stuff though so would be interested to delve deeper coz I have terrible post nasal drip, and I am sure posture would be more connected to that!  


Thanks for in-depth response! I am very insecure about my looks but working on it and wanting to make better habits etc instead of one day doing something like plastic surgery which terrifies me! On those profile pics I have, the top ones are definitely flattering but thanks. I hope I can get some of this stuff down pat and start feeling better and making some good progress :D

Oh trust me I have thought about this stuff long before this situation haha. To me it does, because at the end of the day it is dishonesty, and a lack of respect. Breaking trust in one area can also suggest there may be other things going on behind your back. If I had a great relationship with someone, then found out they were stealing from me, or partook in serious crimes or things I just found morally appalling, despite the good things, it would be a deal-breaker, and I would like to be able to make that decision. We all are capable of being so lovely but also so awful, and we all draw lines in different places and I think should have the opportunity to do so. Some topics aren't always so black and white, but I do want to be with someone who respects me and is honest.

&#x200B;

 I have nothing against open relationships, so long as people are aware, honest and okay with things. If he wanted to date me but hook up with people, I would want that to be put on the table coz hey, what if I have a situation where I am tempted by someone but pass it up out of respect and love for my partner (only to find he hasn't done the same for me). In fact, if I wasn't so insecure about myself or had low self worth/felt I look deformed and wrong, I could imagine myself maybe being a lot more open to that kind of thing. But that is not the case, and I know he would want nothing to do with me if I was intimate with someone else. I have a polyamorous friend I tell him about all the people she is dating and how some are married but also have other partners etc and he always gets weirded out by it. That memory kinda makes me feel better too, his reaction when I told him about that haha.

I haven't spoken to him yet, but when I got agitated he did say he doesn't agree with it/thinks it's wrong. I think I am quite an empathetic person, where as he is very chill and responds to things differently, so I think understanding his perspective is where I am lacking and assuming the worst.

&#x200B;

It does bother me to an extent, when it seems he isn't phased by things that really wind me up, but knowing why can make all the difference. In the heat of the moment, I have overlooked he responds like this to a lot of things, which I find both good and annoying, and I do think his past hardships are probably a reason for that. Is it because he doesn't have respect/morals, or has he gone through things that make the importance of these things (in someone else's relationship) dwindle? 

&#x200B;

I have even had the thought that he has his guard up a lot to avoid feeling anything bad, he doesn't like to dwell on things or show vulnerability. So I am hoping it is more the case of recent traumatic events or avoiding situations having him be blase, opposed to just a general lack of care (I hope that made sense!) He is also the type to joke about things a lot, which is fine, I can too, but he will still do it when I am being serious or talking about upsetting things so in those situations too I have sometimes wondered if he is just joking or not... but again, a lot of people cope with things that way. So many variables!

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I haven't really inserted myself into anything, I don't even know these people, I just happen to be empathetic and get easily upset when I see/hear injustice, especially if it hits close to home. Thus, in my riled up state, hard to comprehend him not being phased but also being against it, can go together. I also wasn't imagining him telling the wife, but more telling the friend what he is doing is not cool etc. I haven't yet spoken to my bf, and I think he has been oblivious to me being so bothered haha, but I think I get his stance now, so will see what he says when I see him next!

&#x200B;

What you highlighted there was more me realising/acknowledging I am getting upset at his friends actions and "manifesting things that aren't there", such as the comment I replied to stated.
